---
import ExpBase from '../../layouts/ExpBase.astro';
import ExpChrome from '../../components/exp/ExpChrome.astro';
import Chatbots from '../../experiments/chatbots/Chatbots';
---

<ExpBase
  title="Chatbots — Frank Young"
  description="Chatbots, 2026 — three simulated conversations sharing one set of components: medical triage, a cat behaviour consultation, and a subscription you cannot cancel. Every response is written by hand, because the subject is the manner of the interface rather than a model behind it. Thinking, no-results, out-of-scope and safety states designed to the same finish as the happy path."
>
  <ExpChrome name="Chatbots" kind="Interface" />
  <main id="main" class="exp-stage">
    <figure class="sb-stage">
      {/* client:visible so the conversation starts when it is scrolled
          to, not on page load — nothing should be halfway through a
          nine-second think before anyone has seen it. */}
      <Chatbots client:visible />

      {/*
        A wall label, not a README. The engineering — the beat union, the
        motive classifier, the three clocks — is in the source and the
        spec, where anyone who wants it will go looking.
      */}
      <figcaption class="sb-label">
        <p class="sb-label__title"><cite>Chatbots</cite>, 2026</p>
        <p class="sb-label__medium">React, CSS modules, no API</p>
        <p class="sb-label__body">
          Three simulated conversations — no actual LLMs were used or consulted in the making.
        </p>
        <p class="sb-label__body">
          The point was to explore how different layouts and components behave inside a
          conversational UI, and to design the awkward states — a wait, a dead end, a
          refusal — to the same finish as the happy path.
        </p>
        {/*
          The engine claim belongs here, a level above the device.

          It was inside the demo, as the cat scenario's own description,
          where it was both the wrong register and the wrong altitude: a
          wall label says what the work IS, and "voice and lexicon are
          data" is a note about how it was made. One level up, addressed
          to someone deciding whether to look, it is exactly the right
          thing to say — and it is only worth saying now that there are
          scripts to prove it.

          The third one is what turns it from a claim into an argument.
          Two cooperative bots look like one bot with two palettes; a
          third that is working against you cannot be explained that
          way, because nothing changed except the authoring.
        */}
        <p class="sb-label__body sb-label__body--dim">
         Always awake, endlessly patient, often useful — and, the second it stops understanding you, this shareholder-friendly design becomes absolutely infuriating. Helpfulness turns out to be a setting, and not always the one shareholders prefer. Three conversations on one engine, and one of them is not on your side. Enjoy the future.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </main>
</ExpBase>

<style>
  /* The device is a white object on a neutral workbench — the ground has
     to be neither the page's near-black nor a panel competing with it. */
  .sb-stage {
    min-height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    padding: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px) 16px;
    background: radial-gradient(120% 70% at 50% 18%, #2a2a2e 0%, #131315 62%, #0c0c0d 100%);
  }
  .sb-label {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .sb-label > p { margin: 0; }
  .sb-label__title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-exp-bright, #c8c8c8);
  }
  .sb-label__title cite { font-style: italic; }
  .sb-label__medium {
    margin-top: 10px !important;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-exp-muted, #9a9a92);
  }
  .sb-label__body {
    margin-top: 18px !important;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-exp-base, #999);
  }
  .sb-label__body--dim {
    margin-top: 14px !important;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-exp-dim, #7d7d75);
  }
</style>
